/-!
# Vanishing above a degree bound on a space with a basis of quasi-compact opens

Let `X` be a quasi-compact topological space whose quasi-compact opens form a basis and are
closed under binary intersection. If `Hᵖ(X, j_!ℤ_U) = 0` for every `p > d` and every
quasi-compact open `j : U → X`, then `Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for every `p > d` and *every* abelian sheaf
`ℱ` on `X`. This is [Stacks, Tag 02UX], a special case of Grothendieck's
[Tohoku, Proposition 3.6.1].

## Main results

* `Stacks.CohomologyVanishing.isZero_cohomology_of_isZero_integerExtensionByZero`: the vanishing
  in the right-derived-global-sections spelling.
* `Stacks.CohomologyVanishing.subsingleton_sheafH_of_subsingleton_sheafH_integerExtensionByZero`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 02UX]**, in the `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.H` spelling of the sibling files in this
  directory.

## The argument

The source's proof, in three reductions, all of them carried out below.

1. *Reduction to subsheaves generated by finitely many sections over quasi-compact opens.*
   A section of `ℱ` over a quasi-compact open `U` is the same thing as a map
   `j_!ℤ_U ⟶ ℱ` (`extensionHomEquivSections`, the `j_! ⊣ j⁻¹` adjunction followed by the
   adjunction defining the constant sheaf), and the subobjects generated by finitely many such
   maps form a filtered family whose supremum is `⊤`, because the quasi-compact opens form a
   basis and therefore those maps are jointly epimorphic (`iSup_finiteSectionSubobject_eq_top`).
   Cohomology over the quasi-compact open `⊤` commutes with that filtered colimit, which is
   [Stacks, Tag 01FF].
2. *Reduction to quotients of a single `j_!ℤ_U`.* A subobject generated by finitely many
   sections is built up one generator at a time; the long exact sequence turns the vanishing for
   such a subobject into the vanishing for the quotients of the individual `j_!ℤ_U`
   (`isZero_finiteSupImages`).
3. *Quotients of `j_!ℤ_U`.* For `0 → 𝒦 → j_!ℤ_U → ℱ → 0` it suffices, by the long exact
   sequence, to kill `𝒦` one degree higher. Now `𝒦` is a subsheaf of the constant sheaf `ℤ`
   (because `j_!ℤ_U` is, by `exists_mono_integerExtensionByZero`), so step 1 applied to `𝒦`
   reduces to subsheaves of `ℤ` generated by finitely many sections over quasi-compact opens,
   and those carry the finite filtration of [Stacks, Tag 0A38] whose successive quotients sit in
   `0 → j'_!ℤ_V → j_!ℤ_U → 𝒬 → 0`. The hypothesis kills the two ends, hence `𝒬`, hence `𝒦`.

## Implementation notes

Cohomology is the right derived functor of global sections,
`(Stacks.Cohomology.AbelianColimit.abSections ⊤).rightDerived p`, and the final statement is
transported to Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.H` by
`Stacks.Cohomology.AbelianColimit.nonempty_H'functor_iso_rightDerived` together with
`Stacks.Cohomology.TerminalCohomology.subsingleton_H_iff_subsingleton_H'_top`, which is how the
sibling vanishing theorems of this directory are spelled.

The long exact sequence is used only through the `CategoryTheory.DeltaFunctor` interface, so the
two-out-of-three vanishing lemmas of the first section below are proved for an arbitrary
cohomological `δ`-functor and then instantiated at
`Stacks.Cohomology.AbelianColimit.cohomologyDeltaFunctor ⊤`.

The commutation of cohomology with filtered colimits is [Stacks, Tag 01FF], which is proved in
the *sheaves of modules* spelling as
`Stacks.Cohomology.Vanishing.isIso_colimit_post_Hfunctor_of_isCompact`. It is transported to
abelian sheaves here by taking for the sheaf of rings the constant sheaf `ℤ`, for which the
underlying-abelian-sheaf functor `SheafOfModules.toSheaf` has a section — an abelian sheaf is a
sheaf of `ℤ`-modules — and by comparing the two cohomologies with [Stacks, Tag 03FD]
(`ModuleSheafCohomology.moduleSheafCohomologyIsoUnderlying`).

All universes are equal: the space is a `TopCat.{u}` and the coefficients are
`AddCommGrpCat.{u}`, which is the spelling of [Stacks, Tag 0A38] and of
`Stacks.Cohomology.Vanishing.isIso_colimit_post_Hfunctor_of_isCompact`, the two inputs that fix
it. The tag has no universe content.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A38](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A38)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01FF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01FF)
* [A. Grothendieck, *Sur quelques points d'algèbre homologique*][Tohoku]
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.Cohomology.AbelianColimit
open Stacks.Sheaves.ConstantIntegerSubsheaves

universe u

namespace Stacks.CohomologyVanishing

/-! ### Two-out-of-three vanishing along a cohomological `δ`-functor -/

section Delta

variable {A : Type*} [Category* A] {B : Type*} [Category* B] [Abelian A] [Abelian B]
  (E : CategoryTheory.DeltaFunctor A B)

/-- If the two outer terms of a short exact sequence vanish in degree `p`, so does the middle
one: exactness of `Eᵖ(A) ⟶ Eᵖ(B) ⟶ Eᵖ(C)`. -/
private lemma isZero_delta_X₂ {S : ShortComplex A} (hS : S.ShortExact) (p : ℕ)
    (h₁ : IsZero ((E.functor p).obj S.X₁))
    (h₃ : IsZero ((E.functor p).obj S.X₃)) :
    IsZero ((E.functor p).obj S.X₂) :=
  (E.exact_map hS p).isZero_X₂_iff.2 ⟨h₁.eq_of_src _ _, h₃.eq_of_tgt _ _⟩

/-- Exactness of `Eᵖ(B) ⟶ Eᵖ(C) ⟶ Eᵖ⁺¹(A)`: the quotient vanishes in degree `p` once the middle
term does and the subobject vanishes in degree `p + 1`. -/
private lemma isZero_delta_X₃ {S : ShortComplex A} (hS : S.ShortExact) (p : ℕ)
    (h₂ : IsZero ((E.functor p).obj S.X₂))
    (h₁ : IsZero ((E.functor (p + 1)).obj S.X₁)) :
    IsZero ((E.functor p).obj S.X₃) :=
  (E.exact_δ₁ hS p).isZero_X₂_iff.2 ⟨h₂.eq_of_src _ _, h₁.eq_of_tgt _ _⟩

/-- A `δ`-functor is additive, so it kills a zero object. -/
private lemma isZero_delta_of_isZero (p : ℕ) {M : A} (hM : IsZero M) :
    IsZero ((E.functor p).obj M) :=
  have := E.additive p
  (E.functor p).map_isZero hM

/-- Vanishing passes across the short exact sequence of a monomorphism and its cokernel. -/
private lemma isZero_delta_of_mono_cokernel {M N : A} (f : M ⟶ N) [Mono f] (p : ℕ)
    (hM : IsZero ((E.functor p).obj M))
    (hC : IsZero ((E.functor p).obj (cokernel f))) :
    IsZero ((E.functor p).obj N) :=
  isZero_delta_X₂ E (S := ShortComplex.cokernelSequence f)
    { exact := ShortComplex.cokernelSequence_exact f
      mono_f := by show Mono f; infer_instance
      epi_g := by dsimp [ShortComplex.cokernelSequence]; infer_instance } p hM hC

/-- Vanishing for a quotient, once its kernel vanishes one degree higher. -/
private lemma isZero_delta_of_epi_kernel {M N : A} (f : M ⟶ N) [Epi f] (p : ℕ)
    (hM : IsZero ((E.functor p).obj M))
    (hK : IsZero ((E.functor (p + 1)).obj (kernel f))) :
    IsZero ((E.functor p).obj N) :=
  isZero_delta_X₃ E (S := ShortComplex.mk (kernel.ι f) f (by simp))
    { exact := ShortComplex.exact_kernel f
      mono_f := by dsimp; infer_instance
      epi_g := by show Epi f; infer_instance } p hM hK

/-- Vanishing along a finite filtration follows from vanishing of its successive quotients. -/
private lemma isZero_delta_of_finiteFiltration (p n : ℕ) (M : Fin (n + 1) → A)
    (f : ∀ i : Fin n, M i.castSucc ⟶ M i.succ) (hf : ∀ i, Mono (f i))
    (hzero : IsZero ((E.functor p).obj (M 0)))
    (hQ : ∀ i, IsZero ((E.functor p).obj (cokernel (f i)))) :
    IsZero ((E.functor p).obj (M (Fin.last n))) := by
  have h : ∀ i : Fin (n + 1), IsZero ((E.functor p).obj (M i)) :=
    Fin.induction hzero (fun i hi => by
      let := hf i
      exact isZero_delta_of_mono_cokernel E (f i) p hi (hQ i))
  exact h (Fin.last n)

end Delta

/-! ### Images, finite suprema of subobjects, and colimits -/

section Subobjects

variable {C : Type*} [Category* C] [Abelian C]

/-- Precomposition by an epimorphism does not change the image subobject. -/
private lemma imageSubobject_comp_eq_of_epi {X' X Y : C} (h : X' ⟶ X) [Epi h] (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    imageSubobject (h ≫ f) = imageSubobject f := by
  let P := imageSubobject (h ≫ f)
  let Q := imageSubobject f
  have hPQ : P ≤ Q := imageSubobject_comp_le h f
  have : Epi (P.ofLE Q hPQ) := inferInstance
  have : IsIso (P.ofLE Q hPQ) :=
    (isIso_iff_mono_and_epi _).2 ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩
  have heq := Subobject.mk_eq_mk_of_comm P.arrow Q.arrow
    (asIso (P.ofLE Q hPQ)) (P.ofLE_arrow hPQ)
  simpa only [Subobject.mk_arrow] using heq

/-- Transport of subobjects along a monomorphism preserves finite suprema. -/
private lemma subobjectMap_finsetSup {M N : C} (e : M ⟶ N) [Mono e]
    {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (S : ι → Subobject M) :
    (Subobject.map e).obj (s.sup S) = s.sup (fun i => (Subobject.map e).obj (S i)) := by
  let a := Subobject.mapPullbackAdj e
  have h : GaloisConnection
      (fun A : Subobject M => (Subobject.map e).obj A)
      (fun B : Subobject N => (Subobject.pullback e).obj B) := fun A B =>
    ⟨fun hAB => leOfHom (a.homEquiv A B (homOfLE hAB)),
      fun hAB => leOfHom ((a.homEquiv A B).symm (homOfLE hAB))⟩
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simpa only [Finset.sup_empty] using (Subobject.map_bot e)
  | @insert i s hi ih => rw [Finset.sup_insert, Finset.sup_insert, h.l_sup, ih]

/-- A map factors through its own image subobject. -/
private lemma imageSubobject_factors_self {X Y : C} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    (imageSubobject f).Factors f := by
  simpa only [Category.id_comp] using imageSubobject_factors_comp_self f (𝟙 _)

/-- The subobject generated by `S.arrow ≫ e` is the image of `S` under `Subobject.map e`. -/
private lemma mk_arrow_comp_eq_map {C' : Type*} [Category* C'] {M N : C'} (S : Subobject M)
    (e : M ⟶ N) [Mono e] :
    Subobject.mk (S.arrow ≫ e) = (Subobject.map e).obj S :=
  (Subobject.map_mk S.arrow e).symm.trans
    (congrArg (fun Q : Subobject M => (Subobject.map e).obj Q) (Subobject.mk_arrow S))

/-- The image of a map postcomposed with a monomorphism is the transported image subobject. -/
private lemma imageSubobject_comp_mono {A M N : C} (f : A ⟶ M) (e : M ⟶ N) [Mono e] :
    imageSubobject (f ≫ e) = (Subobject.map e).obj (imageSubobject f) := by
  let T := imageSubobject f
  have : Mono (T.arrow ≫ e) := inferInstance
  calc
    imageSubobject (f ≫ e) =
        imageSubobject (factorThruImageSubobject f ≫ (T.arrow ≫ e)) := by
          congr 1
          dsimp only [T]
          rw [← Category.assoc, imageSubobject_arrow_comp]
    _ = imageSubobject (T.arrow ≫ e) :=
      imageSubobject_comp_eq_of_epi (factorThruImageSubobject f) (T.arrow ≫ e)
    _ = Subobject.mk (T.arrow ≫ e) := imageSubobject_mono _
    _ = (Subobject.map e).obj T := mk_arrow_comp_eq_map T e

/-- Mapping a subobject along a monomorphism changes only its ambient object. -/
private noncomputable def subobjectMapUnderlyingIso {M N : C} (e : M ⟶ N) [Mono e]
    (S : Subobject M) : (S : C) ≅ ((Subobject.map e).obj S : C) := by
  letI : Mono (S.arrow ≫ e) := inferInstance
  exact (Subobject.underlyingIso (S.arrow ≫ e)).symm ≪≫
    eqToIso (congrArg (fun Q : Subobject N => (Q : C)) (mk_arrow_comp_eq_map S e))

/-- The image of a binary coproduct map is the join of its component images. -/
private lemma imageSubobject_coprod_desc_eq_sup {A B F : C} (f : A ⟶ F) (g : B ⟶ F) :
    imageSubobject (coprod.desc f g) = imageSubobject f ⊔ imageSubobject g := by
  let P : Subobject F := imageSubobject f ⊔ imageSubobject g
  have hF : P.Factors f := Subobject.factors_of_le f le_sup_left (imageSubobject_factors_self f)
  have hG : P.Factors g := Subobject.factors_of_le g le_sup_right (imageSubobject_factors_self g)
  let t : A ⨿ B ⟶ (P : C) := coprod.desc (P.factorThru f hF) (P.factorThru g hG)
  have ht : t ≫ P.arrow = coprod.desc f g := by
    apply coprod.hom_ext
    · simp only [← Category.assoc, t, coprod.inl_desc, P.factorThru_arrow]
    · simp only [← Category.assoc, t, coprod.inr_desc, P.factorThru_arrow]
  apply le_antisymm
  · show imageSubobject (coprod.desc f g) ≤ P
    simpa only [Subobject.mk_arrow] using
      imageSubobject_le_mk P.arrow (coprod.desc f g) t ht
  · apply sup_le
    · calc
        imageSubobject f = imageSubobject (coprod.inl ≫ coprod.desc f g) := by
          rw [coprod.inl_desc]
        _ ≤ imageSubobject (coprod.desc f g) := imageSubobject_comp_le _ _
    · calc
        imageSubobject g = imageSubobject (coprod.inr ≫ coprod.desc f g) := by
          rw [coprod.inr_desc]
        _ ≤ imageSubobject (coprod.desc f g) := imageSubobject_comp_le _ _

/-- If a binary coproduct map is epimorphic, its second component surjects onto the cokernel of
its first component. -/
private lemma epi_comp_cokernel_of_epi_coprod {A E F : C} (a : A ⟶ F) (s : E ⟶ F)
    [Epi (coprod.desc a s)] : Epi (s ≫ cokernel.π a) := by
  let t := coprod.desc a s
  have : Epi (t ≫ cokernel.π a) := inferInstance
  refine ⟨?_⟩
  intro Z g g' hgg'
  apply (cancel_epi (t ≫ cokernel.π a)).1
  apply coprod.hom_ext
  · simp only [t, ← Category.assoc, coprod.inl_desc, cokernel.condition, zero_comp]
  · simpa only [t, ← Category.assoc, coprod.inr_desc] using hgg'

/-- Reindex a finite supremum by the canonical finite type of the finset. -/
private lemma finset_sup_equivFin {β α : Type*} [SemilatticeSup α] [OrderBot α]
    (A : Finset β) (f : β → α) :
    A.sup f = Finset.univ.sup (fun i : Fin A.card => f (A.equivFin.symm i).1) := by
  classical
  apply le_antisymm
  · apply Finset.sup_le
    intro b hb
    let i : Fin A.card := A.equivFin ⟨b, hb⟩
    have hbi : (A.equivFin.symm i).1 = b := by simp [i]
    simpa only [hbi] using
      (Finset.le_sup (s := Finset.univ)
        (f := fun i : Fin A.card => f (A.equivFin.symm i).1) (Finset.mem_univ i))
  · exact Finset.sup_le fun i _ => Finset.le_sup (s := A) (f := f) (A.equivFin.symm i).2

/-- A colimit of zero objects is zero. -/
private lemma isZero_colimit_of_isZero {J : Type*} [Category J]
    {D : Type*} [Category D] [HasZeroMorphisms D] (F : J ⥤ D)
    [HasColimit F] (hF : ∀ j, IsZero (F.obj j)) : IsZero (colimit F) := by
  apply (IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero _).2
  apply colimit.hom_ext
  intro j
  simpa only [Category.comp_id, comp_zero] using (hF j).eq_zero_of_src (colimit.ι F j)

/-- Vanishing passes from every stage of a diagram to its colimit when a functor's canonical
colimit comparison is invertible. -/
private lemma isZero_map_colimit_of_isIso_post {J : Type*} [Category J]
    {D : Type*} [Category D] {D' : Type*} [Category D'] [HasZeroMorphisms D']
    (F : J ⥤ D) (G : D ⥤ D') [HasColimit F] [HasColimit (F ⋙ G)]
    (hpost : IsIso (colimit.post F G))
    (hzero : ∀ j, IsZero (G.obj (F.obj j))) :
    IsZero (G.obj (colimit F)) :=
  (isZero_colimit_of_isZero (F ⋙ G) hzero).of_iso (asIso (colimit.post F G)).symm

/-- A filtered family of subobjects whose supremum is the whole object presents that object as
the colimit of the family. -/
private noncomputable def colimitSubobjectIsoOfiSup {C' : Type*} [Category* C'] [Abelian C']
    [IsGrothendieckAbelian.{u} C'] {J : Type u} [SmallCategory J] [IsFiltered J]
    {M : C'} (D : J ⥤ Subobject M) (hsup : (⨆ j : J, D.obj j) = ⊤) :
    colimit (D ⋙ Subobject.representative ⋙ MonoOver.forget M ⋙ Over.forget M) ≅ M := by
  let F := D ⋙ Subobject.representative
  let B := F ⋙ MonoOver.forget M ⋙ Over.forget M
  let c : Cocone B :=
    { pt := M
      ι :=
        { app j := (F.obj j).obj.hom
          naturality := by
            intro i j g
            change (F.map g).hom.left ≫ (F.obj j).arrow = (F.obj i).arrow ≫ 𝟙 M
            simpa only [Category.comp_id] using (MonoOver.w (F.map g)) } }
  let f : colimit B ⟶ M := colimit.desc B c
  have hf (j : J) : colimit.ι B j ≫ f = (F.obj j).obj.hom := by
    simpa only [f, c] using colimit.ι_desc c j
  haveI : Mono f := IsGrothendieckAbelian.mono_of_isColimit_monoOver F
    (colimit.isColimit B) f hf
  have heq : Subobject.mk f = ⊤ := by
    rw [IsGrothendieckAbelian.subobjectMk_of_isColimit_eq_iSup F (colimit.isColimit B) f hf]
    change (⨆ j : J, Subobject.mk (D.obj j).arrow) = ⊤
    simpa only [Subobject.mk_arrow] using hsup
  haveI : IsIso f := (Subobject.isIso_iff_mk_eq_top f).2 heq
  exact asIso f

end Subobjects

/-! ### Vanishing for a finite supremum of images -/

section SupImages

variable {A : Type*} [Category* A] {B : Type*} [Category* B] [Abelian A] [Abelian B]
  (E : CategoryTheory.DeltaFunctor A B)

/-- Vanishing passes from a subobject and all quotients of one further generator to the object
the two generate. -/
private lemma isZero_delta_of_epi_coprod {M E' F : A} (a : M ⟶ F) [Mono a] (s : E' ⟶ F)
    (hepi : Epi (coprod.desc a s)) (p : ℕ)
    (hA : IsZero ((E.functor p).obj M))
    (hOne : ∀ {Q : A} (g : E' ⟶ Q), Epi g → IsZero ((E.functor p).obj Q)) :
    IsZero ((E.functor p).obj F) := by
  have := hepi
  exact isZero_delta_of_mono_cokernel E a p hA (hOne _ (epi_comp_cokernel_of_epi_coprod a s))

/-- The subobject generated by finitely many maps vanishes in degree `p` as soon as every
quotient of every source does. -/
private lemma isZero_finiteSupImages (p : ℕ) {ι : Type*} (E' : ι → A) {F : A}
    (s : ∀ i, E' i ⟶ F)
    (hOne : ∀ i {Q : A} (f : E' i ⟶ Q), Epi f → IsZero ((E.functor p).obj Q))
    (T : Finset ι) :
    IsZero ((E.functor p).obj ((T.sup (fun i => imageSubobject (s i)) : Subobject F) : A)) := by
  classical
  induction T using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty =>
      simp only [Finset.sup_empty]
      exact isZero_delta_of_isZero E p ((isZero_zero _).of_iso Subobject.botCoeIsoZero)
  | @insert i T hi ih =>
      let P : Subobject F := T.sup (fun j => imageSubobject (s j))
      let t := coprod.desc P.arrow (s i)
      let Q := imageSubobject t
      have hQ : Q = (insert i T).sup (fun j => imageSubobject (s j)) := by
        dsimp only [Q, t]
        rw [imageSubobject_coprod_desc_eq_sup, imageSubobject_mono,
          Subobject.mk_arrow, Finset.sup_insert]
        simp only [P, sup_comm]
      let r := factorThruImageSubobject t
      let a : (P : A) ⟶ (Q : A) := coprod.inl ≫ r
      let b : E' i ⟶ (Q : A) := coprod.inr ≫ r
      have ha : a ≫ Q.arrow = P.arrow := by
        show (coprod.inl ≫ r) ≫ Q.arrow = P.arrow
        rw [Category.assoc, imageSubobject_arrow_comp, coprod.inl_desc]
      have : Mono a := by
        have : Mono (a ≫ Q.arrow) := by rw [ha]; infer_instance
        exact mono_of_mono a Q.arrow
      have hdesc : coprod.desc a b = r := by
        apply coprod.hom_ext
        · simp only [a, coprod.inl_desc]
        · simp only [b, coprod.inr_desc]
      have hepi : Epi (coprod.desc a b) := by rw [hdesc]; infer_instance
      have hz := isZero_delta_of_epi_coprod E a b hepi p ih (hOne i)
      rwa [hQ] at hz

end SupImages

/-! ### Cohomology of abelian sheaves on a space, and filtered colimits -/

section Space

variable (X : TopCat.{u})
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- The cohomological `δ`-functor of global sections of abelian sheaves on `X`: the long exact
cohomology sequence of a short exact sequence of abelian sheaves. Its degree-`p` component is
`(abSections ⊤).rightDerived p`, the `p`-th right derived functor of global sections. -/
noncomputable def globalSectionsDeltaFunctor :
    CategoryTheory.DeltaFunctor (TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  cohomologyDeltaFunctor (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤

/-- The degree-`p` component of `globalSectionsDeltaFunctor` is the `p`-th right derived
functor of global sections. -/
lemma globalSectionsDeltaFunctor_functor (p : ℕ) :
    (globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p =
      (abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).rightDerived p :=
  rfl

omit [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- The quasi-compact opens form an indexed basis. -/
private lemma compactOpens_isBasis (hBasis : PrespectralSpace (X : Type u)) :
    Opens.IsBasis (Set.range (fun U : {U : Opens X // IsCompact (U : Set X)} => U.1)) := by
  obtain ⟨B, hB, hCompact⟩ :
      ∃ B : Set (Set (X : Type u)),
        TopologicalSpace.IsTopologicalBasis B ∧ ∀ U ∈ B, IsCompact U :=
    ⟨_, hBasis.isTopologicalBasis, fun _ hU => hU.2⟩
  refine Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mpr ?_
  intro U x hx
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, hVU⟩ := hB.exists_subset_of_mem_open hx U.2
  exact ⟨⟨V, hB.isOpen hV⟩, ⟨⟨⟨V, hB.isOpen hV⟩, hCompact V hV⟩, rfl⟩, hxV, hVU⟩

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 03FD]** at the terminal open: the cohomology of a sheaf of modules agrees
with the cohomology of its underlying abelian sheaf. -/
private noncomputable def moduleCohomologyIsoUnderlying
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) RingCat.{u})
    (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (p : ℕ) :
    (Hfunctor R ⊤ p).obj M ≅
      ((abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).rightDerived p).obj
        ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).obj M) :=
  ((((ModuleSheafCohomology.moduleSheafCohomologyIsoUnderlying
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) R).choose_spec.2 ⊤).choose) p).app M

/-- [Stacks, Tag 01FF] for sheaves of modules, read as a vanishing statement at `⊤`. -/
private lemma isZero_Hfunctor_filteredColimit
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) RingCat.{u})
    [(Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [EnoughInjectives (SheafOfModules.{u} R)]
    (hX : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set X))
    (hBasis : PrespectralSpace (X : Type u))
    (hInter : QuasiSeparatedSpace (X : Type u))
    {I : Type u} [SmallCategory I] [IsFiltered I]
    (F : I ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u} R) (p : ℕ)
    (hzero : ∀ i, IsZero ((Hfunctor R ⊤ p).obj (F.obj i))) :
    IsZero ((Hfunctor R ⊤ p).obj (colimit F)) :=
  isZero_map_colimit_of_isIso_post F (Hfunctor R ⊤ p)
    (Stacks.Cohomology.Vanishing.isIso_colimit_post_Hfunctor_of_isCompact R hBasis hInter
      F ⊤ hX p) hzero

/-- The sheaf of integers as a sheaf of rings. -/
private noncomputable def integerRingSheaf :
    Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) RingCat.{u} :=
  (sheafCompose (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
    (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat.{u})).obj
      (constantSheafOnSpace X CommRingCat.{u} (CommRingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)))

/-- The constant presheaf of rings `ℤ` mapping to the constant sheaf of rings `ℤ`. -/
private noncomputable def integerRingPresheafToSheaf :
    constantPresheafOnSpace X RingCat.{u} (RingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)) ⟶
      (integerRingSheaf X).obj :=
  Functor.whiskerRight
    (toSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      (constantPresheafOnSpace X CommRingCat.{u} (CommRingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))))
    (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat.{u})

omit [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
private lemma integerRingPresheafToSheaf_locallyInjective :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X) := by
  unfold integerRingPresheafToSheaf
  apply (Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_forget_iff
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) _).mp
  show Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
    (Functor.whiskerRight
      (toSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
        (constantPresheafOnSpace X CommRingCat.{u} (CommRingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))))
      (forget CommRingCat.{u}))
  infer_instance

omit [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
private lemma integerRingPresheafToSheaf_locallySurjective :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X) := by
  unfold integerRingPresheafToSheaf
  apply (Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_whisker_forget
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) _).mpr
  show Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
    (Functor.whiskerRight
      (toSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
        (constantPresheafOnSpace X CommRingCat.{u} (CommRingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))))
      (forget CommRingCat.{u}))
  infer_instance

/-- The sectionwise integer module structure on an abelian sheaf. -/
private noncomputable def abelianSheafAsIntegerPresheaf
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) :
    PresheafOfModules.{u}
      (constantPresheafOnSpace X RingCat.{u} (RingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))) := by
  let R₀ := constantPresheafOnSpace X RingCat.{u} (RingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))
  letI (i : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ) : Module (R₀.obj i) (F.obj.obj i) := by
    change Module (ULift.{u} ℤ) (F.obj.obj i)
    infer_instance
  exact PresheafOfModules.ofPresheaf F.obj (by
    intro A B f r m
    dsimp [R₀, constantPresheafOnSpace]
    exact map_zsmul (F.obj.map f).hom r.down m)

private noncomputable def abelianSheafAsIntegerPresheafFunctor :
    TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X ⥤
      PresheafOfModules.{u}
        (constantPresheafOnSpace X RingCat.{u} (RingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))) where
  obj := abelianSheafAsIntegerPresheaf X
  map {F G} f := PresheafOfModules.homMk f.hom (by
    intro A r m
    change (f.hom.app A).hom (r.down • m) = r.down • (f.hom.app A).hom m
    exact map_zsmul (f.hom.app A).hom r.down m)
  map_id F := by
    ext A x
    rfl
  map_comp f g := by
    ext A x
    rfl

/-- An abelian sheaf, read as a sheaf of modules over the constant sheaf of rings `ℤ`. -/
private noncomputable def abelianSheafAsIntegerModuleFunctor :
    TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u} (integerRingSheaf X) := by
  letI : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X) := integerRingPresheafToSheaf_locallyInjective X
  letI : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X) := integerRingPresheafToSheaf_locallySurjective X
  exact abelianSheafAsIntegerPresheafFunctor X ⋙
    PresheafOfModules.sheafification (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X)

/-- Reading an abelian sheaf as a sheaf of `ℤ`-modules does not change it. -/
private noncomputable def abelianSheafAsIntegerModuleFunctorUnderlyingIso :
    abelianSheafAsIntegerModuleFunctor X ⋙ SheafOfModules.toSheaf (integerRingSheaf X) ≅
      𝟭 (TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) := by
  let J := Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)
  letI : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X) :=
    integerRingPresheafToSheaf_locallyInjective X
  letI : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X) :=
    integerRingPresheafToSheaf_locallySurjective X
  let R₀ := constantPresheafOnSpace X RingCat.{u} (RingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))
  let H := abelianSheafAsIntegerPresheafFunctor X
  let L := PresheafOfModules.sheafification (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X)
  let T := SheafOfModules.toSheaf (integerRingSheaf X)
  let Ev := PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R₀
  let S := presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}
  have hHE : H ⋙ Ev ≅ sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u} := Iso.refl _
  have hML : abelianSheafAsIntegerModuleFunctor X = H ⋙ L := rfl
  rw [hML]
  let e : sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u} ⋙ S ≅ 𝟭 (TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) :=
    @asIso _ _ _ _ (sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).counit
      CategoryTheory.sheafification_reflective
  exact (Functor.associator H L T) ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerLeft H (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationCompToSheaf
      (integerRingPresheafToSheaf X)) ≪≫
    (Functor.associator H Ev S).symm ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight hHE S ≪≫ e

/-- Forgetting a sheaf of modules to its underlying abelian sheaf preserves colimits. -/
private lemma toSheaf_preservesColimits
    (O : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) RingCat.{u}) :
    PreservesColimits (SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{u, u, u, u} O) := by
  let L := PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 O.obj)
  let adj : L ⊣ _ := PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (𝟙 O.obj)
  have hL : PreservesColimits L := adj.leftAdjoint_preservesColimits
  have hLT : PreservesColimits (L ⋙ SheafOfModules.toSheaf O) :=
    preservesColimits_of_natIso (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationCompToSheaf (𝟙 O.obj)).symm
  refine ⟨?_⟩
  intro J _
  refine ⟨?_⟩
  intro D
  refine ⟨?_⟩
  intro c hc
  let Res := SheafOfModules.forget O ⋙ PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars (𝟙 O.obj)
  have e : (D ⋙ Res) ⋙ L ≅ D :=
    NatIso.ofComponents (fun j => (asIso adj.counit).app (D.obj j)) (by
      intro i j f
      exact (asIso adj.counit).hom.naturality (D.map f))
  have h1 : PreservesColimit (D ⋙ Res) L := hL.preservesColimitsOfShape.preservesColimit
  have h2 : PreservesColimit (D ⋙ Res) (L ⋙ SheafOfModules.toSheaf O) :=
    hLT.preservesColimitsOfShape.preservesColimit
  have hpc : PreservesColimit ((D ⋙ Res) ⋙ L) (SheafOfModules.toSheaf O) :=
    preservesColimit_of_preserves_colimit_cocone
      (isColimitOfPreserves L (colimit.isColimit (D ⋙ Res)))
      (isColimitOfPreserves (L ⋙ SheafOfModules.toSheaf O) (colimit.isColimit (D ⋙ Res)))
  have hD := preservesColimit_of_iso_diagram (SheafOfModules.toSheaf O) e
  exact ⟨isColimitOfPreserves (SheafOfModules.toSheaf O) hc⟩

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 01FF] for abelian sheaves at the terminal open.** On a quasi-compact space
with a basis of quasi-compact opens closed under binary intersection, cohomology of abelian
sheaves commutes with filtered colimits, so vanishing at every stage gives vanishing at the
colimit. -/
private lemma isZero_cohomology_filteredColimit
    (hX : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set X))
    (hBasis : PrespectralSpace (X : Type u))
    (hInter : QuasiSeparatedSpace (X : Type u))
    {I : Type u} [SmallCategory I] [IsFiltered I]
    (D : I ⥤ TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) [HasColimit D] (p : ℕ)
    (hzero : ∀ i, IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj (D.obj i))) :
    IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj
      (@colimit _ _ _ _ D ‹HasColimit D›)) := by
  let O := integerRingSheaf X
  let H := abelianSheafAsIntegerModuleFunctor X
  let T := SheafOfModules.toSheaf O
  let MD := D ⋙ H
  let G := (abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤)
  have : EnoughInjectives (SheafOfModules.{u} O) := IsGrothendieckAbelian.enoughInjectives
  have hzeroMD (i : I) : IsZero ((Hfunctor O ⊤ p).obj (MD.obj i)) := by
    have hz : IsZero ((G.rightDerived p).obj (T.obj (MD.obj i))) :=
      (hzero i).of_iso ((G.rightDerived p).mapIso
        ((abelianSheafAsIntegerModuleFunctorUnderlyingIso X).app (D.obj i)))
    exact hz.of_iso (moduleCohomologyIsoUnderlying X O (MD.obj i) p)
  have hM : IsZero ((Hfunctor O ⊤ p).obj (colimit MD)) :=
    isZero_Hfunctor_filteredColimit X O hX hBasis hInter MD p hzeroMD
  have hA : IsZero ((G.rightDerived p).obj (T.obj (colimit MD))) :=
    hM.of_iso (moduleCohomologyIsoUnderlying X O (colimit MD) p).symm
  have : PreservesColimits T := toSheaf_preservesColimits X O
  let η : MD ⋙ T ≅ D :=
    (Functor.associator D H T) ≪≫
      Functor.isoWhiskerLeft D (abelianSheafAsIntegerModuleFunctorUnderlyingIso X) ≪≫
      D.rightUnitor
  let e : T.obj (colimit MD) ≅ @colimit _ _ _ _ D ‹HasColimit D› :=
    preservesColimitIso T MD ≪≫ colim.mapIso η
  exact hA.of_iso ((G.rightDerived p).mapIso e).symm

end Space

/-! ### Sections over a quasi-compact open as maps out of `j_!ℤ_U` -/

section Sections

variable (X : TopCat.{u}) (U : Opens X)
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- A map out of `j_!ℤ_U` is the same thing as a section of the restriction to `U`: the
composite of the `j_! ⊣ j⁻¹` adjunction with the adjunction defining the constant sheaf. -/
private noncomputable def extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections
    [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
      (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) :
    (integerExtensionByZero X U ⟶ F) ≃
      ((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj F).obj.obj
        (op (⊤ : Opens (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U))) := by
  let J := Opens.grothendieckTopology (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)
  let Eℤ := constantSheafOnSpace (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U)
    AddCommGrpCat.{u} (AddCommGrpCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))
  let R := (Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj F
  let e₁ := (TopCat.Presheaf.extendByInitialSheafAdjunction U).homEquiv Eℤ F
  let e₂ := (constantSheafAdj J AddCommGrpCat.{u}
    (T := ⊤) (IsTerminal.ofUniqueHom (fun _ => homOfLE le_top) (fun _ _ => rfl))).homEquiv
      (AddCommGrpCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)) R
  exact e₁.trans (e₂.trans (AddCommGrpCat.uliftZMultiplesAddEquiv _).toEquiv)

private lemma extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections_comp
    [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
      (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    {F G : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X} (f : F ⟶ G)
    (s : integerExtensionByZero X U ⟶ F) :
    extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections X U G (s ≫ f) =
      (((Opens.sheafRestrict U).map f).hom.app (op ⊤))
        (extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections X U F s) := by
  let Eℤ := constantSheafOnSpace (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U)
    AddCommGrpCat.{u} (AddCommGrpCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))
  let J := Opens.grothendieckTopology (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)
  let α := TopCat.Presheaf.extendByInitialSheafAdjunction (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) U
  let β := constantSheafAdj J AddCommGrpCat.{u}
    (T := ⊤) (IsTerminal.ofUniqueHom (fun _ => homOfLE le_top) (fun _ _ => rfl))
  let rf := (Opens.sheafRestrict U).map f
  have h₁ : (α.homEquiv Eℤ G) (s ≫ f) = (α.homEquiv Eℤ F) s ≫ rf :=
    α.homEquiv_naturality_right s f
  have h₂ : (β.homEquiv _ ((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj G)) ((α.homEquiv Eℤ F) s ≫ rf) =
      (β.homEquiv _ ((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj F)) ((α.homEquiv Eℤ F) s) ≫
        ((sheafSections J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (op ⊤)).map rf :=
    β.homEquiv_naturality_right _ rf
  let γF := (AddCommGrpCat.uliftZMultiplesAddEquiv
    (((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj F).obj.obj (op ⊤))).toEquiv
  let γG := (AddCommGrpCat.uliftZMultiplesAddEquiv
    (((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj G).obj.obj (op ⊤))).toEquiv
  show γG ((β.homEquiv _ ((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj G)) ((α.homEquiv Eℤ G) (s ≫ f))) =
      rf.hom.app (op ⊤) (γF ((β.homEquiv _ ((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj F))
        ((α.homEquiv Eℤ F) s)))
  rw [h₁]
  apply Eq.trans (congrArg γG h₂)
  rfl

/-- Restriction to an open subset carries the constant abelian sheaf to the constant abelian
sheaf. -/
private noncomputable def restrictConstantSheafIso
    [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
      (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] :
    constantSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u} ⋙
      Opens.sheafRestrict U ≅
      constantSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology
        (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u} := by
  let hX : IsTerminal (⊤ : Opens X) :=
    IsTerminal.ofUniqueHom (fun _ => homOfLE le_top) (fun _ _ => rfl)
  let hU : IsTerminal (⊤ : Opens (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U)) :=
    IsTerminal.ofUniqueHom (fun _ => homOfLE le_top) (fun _ _ => rfl)
  let aX := constantSheafAdj (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u} hX
  let aU := constantSheafAdj
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u))
    AddCommGrpCat.{u} hU
  let aR := TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sheafRestrictPushforwardAdjunction
    (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) U
  let aComp := aX.comp aR
  change _ ⊣ (sheafSections
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u))
    AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (op ⊤) at aComp
  exact aComp.leftAdjointUniq aU

omit [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- The counit from the presheaf extension by zero of a restriction is componentwise monic. -/
private lemma mono_presheafExtensionCounit (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) :
    Mono (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.homEquivInv U
      (𝟙 ((TopCat.Presheaf.restrictToOpen U).obj F.obj))) := by
  let P := (TopCat.Presheaf.restrictToOpen U).obj F.obj
  let f := TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.homEquivInv U (𝟙 P)
  show Mono f
  have : ∀ V, Mono (f.app V) := fun V => by
    by_cases hV : V.unop ≤ U
    · have hi : IsIso (f.app V) := by
        show IsIso (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.homEquivInvApp U (𝟙 P) V)
        rw [TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.homEquivInvApp, dite_eq_left hV]
        infer_instance
      infer_instance
    · show Mono (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.homEquivInvApp U (𝟙 P) V)
      rw [TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.homEquivInvApp, dite_eq_right hV]
      exact (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.isInitial_obj U P hV).isZero.mono _
  exact NatTrans.mono_of_mono_app f

/-- The extension by zero of the restriction of an abelian sheaf is a subsheaf of it. -/
private lemma exists_mono_extensionRestrict (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) :
    ∃ f : (TopCat.Presheaf.extendByInitialSheaf U).obj ((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj F) ⟶ F,
      Mono f := by
  let J := Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)
  let P := (TopCat.Presheaf.restrictToOpen U).obj F.obj
  let fp := TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.homEquivInv U (𝟙 P)
  let S := presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}
  let f : (TopCat.Presheaf.extendByInitialSheaf U).obj ((Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj F) ⟶ F :=
    S.map fp ≫ (sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).counit.app F
  have : Mono fp := mono_presheafExtensionCounit X U F
  let : PreservesFiniteLimits S := inferInstance
  have : Mono (S.map fp) := inferInstance
  have : IsIso (sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).counit :=
    CategoryTheory.sheafification_reflective
  have : IsIso ((sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).counit.app F) :=
    NatIso.isIso_app_of_isIso _ _
  have : Mono ((sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).counit.app F) := inferInstance
  exact ⟨f, mono_comp' (inferInstanceAs (Mono (S.map fp)))
    (inferInstanceAs (Mono ((sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).counit.app F)))⟩

/-- **`j_!ℤ_U` is a subsheaf of the constant sheaf `ℤ`.** -/
private lemma exists_mono_integerExtensionByZero
    [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
      (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] :
    ∃ f : integerExtensionByZero X U ⟶ integerConstantSheaf X, Mono f := by
  let A := AddCommGrpCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)
  let Cst := constantSheafOnSpace X AddCommGrpCat.{u} A
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_mono_extensionRestrict X U Cst
  let e : constantSheafOnSpace (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U)
      AddCommGrpCat.{u} A ≅ (Opens.sheafRestrict U).obj Cst :=
    ((restrictConstantSheafIso X U).app A).symm
  have : IsIso e.hom := e.isIso_hom
  have : IsIso ((TopCat.Presheaf.extendByInitialSheaf U).map e.hom) := by
    show IsIso (((TopCat.Presheaf.extendByInitialSheaf U).mapIso e).hom); infer_instance
  exact ⟨(TopCat.Presheaf.extendByInitialSheaf U).map e.hom ≫ g,
    mono_comp' (inferInstanceAs (Mono ((TopCat.Presheaf.extendByInitialSheaf U).map e.hom))) hg⟩

/-- **A map `j_!ℤ_U ⟶ ℱ` is the same thing as a section of `ℱ` over `U`.** -/
private noncomputable def extensionHomEquivSections
    [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
      (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) :
    (integerExtensionByZero X U ⟶ F) ≃ F.obj.obj (op U) := by
  let i : op ((TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.imF U).obj ⊤) ⟶ op U :=
    eqToHom (congrArg op (Opens.isOpenEmbedding_obj_top U))
  exact (extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections X U F).trans
    (Equiv.ofBijective (F.obj.map i) (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (F.obj.map i)))

private lemma extensionHomEquivSections_comp
    [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
      (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    {F G : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X} (f : F ⟶ G)
    (s : integerExtensionByZero X U ⟶ F) :
    extensionHomEquivSections X U G (s ≫ f) =
      f.hom.app (op U) (extensionHomEquivSections X U F s) := by
  dsimp [extensionHomEquivSections]
  rw [extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections_comp]
  exact (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (f.hom.naturality
    (eqToHom (congrArg op (Opens.isOpenEmbedding_obj_top U))))
      (extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections X U F s)).symm

end Sections

/-! ### The vanishing theorem -/

section Main

variable (X : TopCat.{u})
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ U : Opens X, HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
    (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- Maps out of the sheaves `j_!ℤ_U` for quasi-compact `U` are jointly epimorphic: they detect
equality of morphisms of abelian sheaves. -/
private lemma compactExtensions_isSeparating (hBasis : PrespectralSpace (X : Type u))
    {F G : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X} (f g : F ⟶ G)
    (h : ∀ (U : Opens X), IsCompact (U : Set X) →
      ∀ s : integerExtensionByZero X U ⟶ F, s ≫ f = s ≫ g) : f = g := by
  apply Sheaf.hom_ext
  apply TopCat.Sheaf.hom_ext F.obj G (compactOpens_isBasis X hBasis)
  intro U
  have heq : ((Opens.sheafRestrict U.1).map f).hom.app (op ⊤) =
      ((Opens.sheafRestrict U.1).map g).hom.app (op ⊤) := by
    ext y
    let e := extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections X U.1 F
    let s := e.symm y
    have hs := h U.1 U.2 s
    have hs' := congrArg (extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections X U.1 G) hs
    rw [extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections_comp,
      extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections_comp] at hs'
    have hy : (extensionHomEquivRestrictedSections X U.1 F) s = y :=
      Equiv.apply_symm_apply _ _
    rwa [hy] at hs'
  change f.hom.app (op (U.1.isOpenEmbedding.functor.obj ⊤)) =
    g.hom.app (op (U.1.isOpenEmbedding.functor.obj ⊤)) at heq
  rwa [Opens.isOpenEmbedding_obj_top] at heq

/-- The subobject of `ℱ` generated by a finite set of sections over quasi-compact opens. -/
private noncomputable def finiteSectionSubobject (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X)
    (A : Finset (Σ U : Opens X, {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)})) :
    Subobject F :=
  A.sup (fun a => imageSubobject ((extensionHomEquivSections X a.1 F).symm a.2.1))

private lemma finiteSectionSubobject_mono (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X)
    {A B : Finset (Σ U : Opens X, {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)})}
    (hAB : A ⊆ B) :
    finiteSectionSubobject X F A ≤ finiteSectionSubobject X F B :=
  Finset.sup_mono hAB

/-- The finite section subobjects of `ℱ`, as a filtered diagram of subobjects. -/
private noncomputable def finiteSectionDiagram (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) :
    Finset (Σ U : Opens X, {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)}) ⥤ Subobject F :=
  (show Monotone (finiteSectionSubobject X F) from
    fun _ _ h => finiteSectionSubobject_mono X F h).functor

omit [∀ U : Opens X, HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
  (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- A finite supremum of images of maps `j_!ℤ_{Uᵢ} ⟶ ℤ` over quasi-compact opens is finitely
generated by sections over quasi-compact opens in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 0A38]. -/
private lemma finitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections_supImages
    (n : ℕ) (U : Fin n → Opens X) (hU : ∀ i, IsCompact (U i : Set X))
    (s : ∀ i, integerExtensionByZero X (U i) ⟶ integerConstantSheaf X) :
    FinitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections X
      (Finset.univ.sup (fun i => imageSubobject (s i))) := by
  let F : Subobject (integerConstantSheaf X) :=
    Finset.univ.sup (fun i => imageSubobject (s i))
  have hf (i : Fin n) : F.Factors (s i) := by
    apply Subobject.finset_sup_factors
    exact ⟨i, Finset.mem_univ i, imageSubobject_factors_self (s i)⟩
  refine ⟨n, U, hU, (fun i => F.factorThru (s i) (hf i)), ?_⟩
  show Finset.univ.sup (fun i => imageSubobject (F.factorThru (s i) (hf i) ≫ F.arrow)) = F
  simp only [Subobject.factorThru_arrow]
  rfl

omit [∀ U : Opens X, HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
  (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- Finite generation by sections over quasi-compact opens is retained when the generated
subobject is pushed into the constant sheaf `ℤ`. -/
private lemma finitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections_map
    (M : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) (e : M ⟶ integerConstantSheaf X) [Mono e]
    (n : ℕ) (U : Fin n → Opens X) (hU : ∀ i, IsCompact (U i : Set X))
    (s : ∀ i, integerExtensionByZero X (U i) ⟶ M) :
    FinitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections X
      ((Subobject.map e).obj (Finset.univ.sup (fun i => imageSubobject (s i)))) := by
  have hEq : (Subobject.map e).obj (Finset.univ.sup (fun i => imageSubobject (s i))) =
      Finset.univ.sup (fun i => imageSubobject (s i ≫ e)) := by
    rw [subobjectMap_finsetSup]
    congr 1
    funext i
    exact (imageSubobject_comp_mono (s i) e).symm
  rw [hEq]
  exact finitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections_supImages X n U hU (fun i => s i ≫ e)

private lemma finitelyGenerated_finiteSectionSubobject_map
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) (e : F ⟶ integerConstantSheaf X) [Mono e]
    (A : Finset (Σ U : Opens X, {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)})) :
    FinitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections X
      ((Subobject.map e).obj (finiteSectionSubobject X F A)) := by
  let a : Fin A.card → Σ U : Opens X, {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)} :=
    fun i => (A.equivFin.symm i).1
  let U : Fin A.card → Opens X := fun i => (a i).1
  let s : ∀ i, integerExtensionByZero X (U i) ⟶ F :=
    fun i => (extensionHomEquivSections X (U i) F).symm (a i).2.1
  have hA : finiteSectionSubobject X F A =
      Finset.univ.sup (fun i : Fin A.card => imageSubobject (s i)) := by
    unfold finiteSectionSubobject
    rw [finset_sup_equivFin]
  rw [hA]
  exact finitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections_map X F e A.card U (fun i => (a i).2.2) s

/-- **The finite section subobjects exhaust `ℱ`.** This is where the hypothesis that the
quasi-compact opens form a basis enters. -/
private lemma iSup_finiteSectionSubobject_eq_top (hBasis : PrespectralSpace (X : Type u))
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) :
    (⨆ A : Finset (Σ U : Opens X, {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)}),
      finiteSectionSubobject X F A) = ⊤ := by
  let P : Subobject F := ⨆ A : Finset (Σ U : Opens X,
    {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)}), finiteSectionSubobject X F A
  have hfac (U : Opens X) (hU : IsCompact (U : Set X))
      (s : integerExtensionByZero X U ⟶ F) : P.Factors s := by
    let a : Σ U : Opens X, {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)} :=
      ⟨U, ⟨extensionHomEquivSections X U F s, hU⟩⟩
    have hs : (extensionHomEquivSections X U F).symm a.2.1 = s := Equiv.symm_apply_apply _ _
    have hImage :
        (imageSubobject ((extensionHomEquivSections X U F).symm a.2.1)).Factors s := by
      rw [hs]
      exact imageSubobject_factors_self s
    have hStage : (finiteSectionSubobject X F {a}).Factors s :=
      Subobject.finset_sup_factors ⟨a, Finset.mem_singleton_self a, hImage⟩
    exact Subobject.factors_of_le s (le_iSup (fun A => finiteSectionSubobject X F A) {a}) hStage
  have : Epi P.arrow := ⟨by
    intro G f g hfg
    apply compactExtensions_isSeparating X hBasis f g
    intro U hU s
    rw [← P.factorThru_arrow s (hfac U hU s), Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hfg]⟩
  simpa only [Subobject.mk_arrow] using (Subobject.epi_iff_mk_eq_top P.arrow).mp inferInstance

/-- **Hypothesis (4) of [Stacks, Tag 02UX]**: `Hᵖ(X, j_!ℤ_U) = 0` for every `p > d` and every
quasi-compact open `U ⊆ X`. -/
def IsZeroIntegerExtensions (d : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ U : Opens X, IsCompact (U : Set X) → ∀ p : ℕ, d < p →
    IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj (integerExtensionByZero X U))

variable (hX : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set X))
  (hBasis : PrespectralSpace (X : Type u))
  (hInter : QuasiSeparatedSpace (X : Type u))

include hX hBasis hInter

/-- **Reduction 1.** Vanishing for every finite section subobject gives vanishing for `ℱ`:
the finite section subobjects are a filtered family with supremum `⊤`, and cohomology over the
quasi-compact open `⊤` commutes with filtered colimits ([Stacks, Tag 01FF]). -/
private lemma isZero_of_finiteSectionSubobjects
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) (p : ℕ)
    (hzero : ∀ A : Finset (Σ U : Opens X,
        {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)}),
      IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj
        (finiteSectionSubobject X F A : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X))) :
    IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj F) := by
  let D := finiteSectionDiagram X F
  let B := D ⋙ Subobject.representative ⋙ MonoOver.forget F ⋙ Over.forget F
  let : HasColimit B := inferInstance
  let e : colimit B ≅ F :=
    colimitSubobjectIsoOfiSup D (iSup_finiteSectionSubobject_eq_top X hBasis F)
  have hc : IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj
      (@colimit _ _ _ _ B ‹HasColimit B›)) :=
    isZero_cohomology_filteredColimit X hX hBasis hInter B p hzero
  exact hc.of_iso (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).mapIso e).symm

variable [QuasiSeparatedSpace (X : Type u)]

omit [∀ U : Opens X, HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
  (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] hX hBasis hInter in
/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0A38] feeds the hypothesis.** A subsheaf of the constant sheaf `ℤ` generated
by finitely many sections over quasi-compact opens has vanishing cohomology above `d`: its
finite filtration has successive quotients squeezed between two sheaves `j_!ℤ_V` and `j_!ℤ_U`
over quasi-compact opens, which the hypothesis kills. -/
private lemma isZero_finitelyGeneratedSubobject
    (d : ℕ) (hvanish : IsZeroIntegerExtensions X d)
    (F : Subobject (integerConstantSheaf X))
    (hF : FinitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections X F) (p : ℕ) (hp : d < p) :
    IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj
      (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X)) := by
  obtain ⟨n, H, hH, hzero, hlast, hstep⟩ :=
    exists_filtration_of_finitelyGeneratedByCompactOpenSections X F hF
  have hQ (i : Fin n) :
      IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj
        (cokernel (Subobject.ofLE (H i.castSucc) (H i.succ) (hH i.castSucc_le_succ)))) := by
    obtain ⟨U, V, hVU, hU, hV, a, b, hab, hs⟩ := hstep i
    exact isZero_delta_X₃ (globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X) hs p (hvanish U hU p hp)
      (hvanish V hV (p + 1) (by omega))
  have hfirst : IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj
      (H 0 : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X)) := by
    rw [hzero]
    exact isZero_delta_of_isZero (globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X) p
      ((isZero_zero _).of_iso Subobject.botCoeIsoZero)
  have hresult := isZero_delta_of_finiteFiltration (globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X) p n
    (fun i => (H i : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X))
    (fun i => Subobject.ofLE (H i.castSucc) (H i.succ) (hH i.castSucc_le_succ))
    (fun i => inferInstance) hfirst hQ
  simpa only [hlast] using hresult

omit hX hBasis hInter in
/-- A finite section subobject of a sheaf embedded in the constant sheaf `ℤ` has vanishing
cohomology above `d`. -/
private lemma isZero_finiteSectionSubobject_of_mono_constant
    (d : ℕ) (hvanish : IsZeroIntegerExtensions X d)
    (K : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) (e : K ⟶ integerConstantSheaf X) [Mono e]
    (A : Finset (Σ U : Opens X, {_s : K.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)}))
    (p : ℕ) (hp : d < p) :
    IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj
      (finiteSectionSubobject X K A : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X)) := by
  have hz := isZero_finitelyGeneratedSubobject X d hvanish
    ((Subobject.map e).obj (finiteSectionSubobject X K A))
    (finitelyGenerated_finiteSectionSubobject_map X K e A) p hp
  exact hz.of_iso (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).mapIso
    (subobjectMapUnderlyingIso e (finiteSectionSubobject X K A)))

/-- **Reduction 3, first half.** A subsheaf of the constant sheaf `ℤ` has vanishing cohomology
above `d`: reduce to the finitely generated case by Reduction 1. -/
private lemma isZero_of_mono_integerConstant
    (d : ℕ) (hvanish : IsZeroIntegerExtensions X d)
    (K : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) (e : K ⟶ integerConstantSheaf X) [Mono e]
    (p : ℕ) (hp : d < p) :
    IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj K) := by
  refine isZero_of_finiteSectionSubobjects X hX hBasis hInter K p (fun A => ?_)
  exact isZero_finiteSectionSubobject_of_mono_constant X d hvanish K e A p hp

/-- **Reduction 3, second half.** Every quotient of `j_!ℤ_U` over a quasi-compact open `U` has
vanishing cohomology above `d`: the kernel is a subsheaf of the constant sheaf `ℤ`. -/
private lemma isZero_quotientOfIntegerExtension
    (d : ℕ) (hvanish : IsZeroIntegerExtensions X d)
    (U : Opens X) (hU : IsCompact (U : Set X))
    {F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X} (f : integerExtensionByZero X U ⟶ F) [Epi f]
    (p : ℕ) (hp : d < p) :
    IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj F) := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_mono_integerExtensionByZero X U
  let : Mono e := he
  have : Mono (kernel.ι f ≫ e) := mono_comp' (inferInstanceAs (Mono (kernel.ι f))) he
  have hK := isZero_of_mono_integerConstant X hX hBasis hInter d hvanish
    (kernel f) (kernel.ι f ≫ e) (p + 1) (by omega)
  exact isZero_delta_of_epi_kernel (globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X) f p (hvanish U hU p hp) hK

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 02UX], in the right-derived-global-sections spelling.** Let `X` be a
quasi-compact topological space whose quasi-compact opens form a basis and are closed under
binary intersection. If `Hᵖ(X, j_!ℤ_U) = 0` for all `p > d` and every quasi-compact open `U`,
then `Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for all `p > d` and every abelian sheaf `ℱ` on `X`. -/
theorem isZero_cohomology_of_isZero_integerExtensionByZero
    (d : ℕ) (hvanish : IsZeroIntegerExtensions X d)
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) (p : ℕ) (hp : d < p) :
    IsZero ((abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).rightDerived p |>.obj F) := by
  refine isZero_of_finiteSectionSubobjects X hX hBasis hInter F p (fun A => ?_)
  let I := Σ U : Opens X, {_s : F.obj.obj (op U) // IsCompact (U : Set X)}
  let Ext' : I → TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X :=
    fun a => integerExtensionByZero X a.1
  let s : ∀ a : I, Ext' a ⟶ F := fun a => (extensionHomEquivSections X a.1 F).symm a.2.1
  have hOne (a : I) {Q : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X} (f : Ext' a ⟶ Q) (hf : Epi f) :
      IsZero (((globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X).functor p).obj Q) := by
    let : Epi f := hf
    exact isZero_quotientOfIntegerExtension X hX hBasis hInter d hvanish a.1 a.2.2 f p hp
  exact isZero_finiteSupImages (globalSectionsDeltaFunctor X) p Ext' s hOne A

end Main

/-! ### The tag, in the `Sheaf.H` spelling -/

section SheafH

variable (X : TopCat.{u})
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ U : Opens X, HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
    (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u})]

omit [∀ U : Opens X, HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology
  (TopCat.Presheaf.ExtensionByInitial.sp U : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.H` vanishes exactly when the right derived functor of
global sections does: the two are the same group up to isomorphism, by
`Stacks.Cohomology.TerminalCohomology.subsingleton_H_iff_subsingleton_H'_top` and
`Stacks.Cohomology.AbelianColimit.nonempty_H'functor_iso_rightDerived`. -/
lemma subsingleton_sheafH_iff_isZero_rightDerived
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) (p : ℕ) :
    Subsingleton (Sheaf.H.{u, u, u, u} F p) ↔
      IsZero (((abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).rightDerived p).obj F) := by
  refine (Stacks.Cohomology.TerminalCohomology.subsingleton_H_iff_subsingleton_H'_top
    (X := (X : Type u)) F p).trans ?_
  have e := (nonempty_H'functor_iso_rightDerived (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤ p).some.app F
  exact ⟨fun h => (AddCommGrpCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton.2 h).of_iso e.symm,
    fun h => AddCommGrpCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton.1 (h.of_iso e)⟩

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 02UX]** (a special case of [Tohoku, Proposition 3.6.1]). Let `X` be a
topological space and let `d ≥ 0` be an integer. Assume

1. `X` is quasi-compact,
2. the quasi-compact opens form a basis for `X`,
3. the intersection of two quasi-compact opens is quasi-compact, and
4. `Hᵖ(X, j_!ℤ_U) = 0` for all `p > d` and any quasi-compact open `j : U → X`.

Then `Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for all `p > d` and any abelian sheaf `ℱ` on `X`. -/
@[stacks 02UX]
theorem subsingleton_sheafH_of_subsingleton_sheafH_integerExtensionByZero (d : ℕ)
    (hX : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set X))
    (hBasis : PrespectralSpace (X : Type u))
    (hInter : QuasiSeparatedSpace (X : Type u))
    (hvanish : ∀ U : Opens X, IsCompact (U : Set X) → ∀ p : ℕ, d < p →
      Subsingleton (Sheaf.H.{u, u, u, u} (integerExtensionByZero X U) p))
    (F : TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} X) (p : ℕ) (hp : d < p) :
    Subsingleton (Sheaf.H.{u, u, u, u} F p) := by
  refine (subsingleton_sheafH_iff_isZero_rightDerived X F p).2 ?_
  refine isZero_cohomology_of_isZero_integerExtensionByZero X hX hBasis hInter d ?_ F p hp
  intro U hU q hq
  exact (subsingleton_sheafH_iff_isZero_rightDerived X _ q).1 (hvanish U hU q hq)

end SheafH

end Stacks.CohomologyVanishing

end
